WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.085
- America.

00:00:01.085 --> 00:00:03.462
Land of the free, home of the brave.

00:00:03.462 --> 00:00:06.131
You've got some great
things like barbecue,

00:00:06.131 --> 00:00:08.133
baseball, a hip president,

00:00:08.133 --> 00:00:11.345
but here are some things
you're doing bloody wrong.

00:00:11.345 --> 00:00:13.254
(classical music)

00:00:13.254 --> 00:00:14.431
Roundabouts.

00:00:14.431 --> 00:00:16.016
You just don't have enough of them.

00:00:16.016 --> 00:00:17.643
Wouldn't you rather deal with this

00:00:17.643 --> 00:00:19.120
than this?

00:00:19.120 --> 00:00:20.187
Food.

00:00:20.187 --> 00:00:21.689
American pancakes.

00:00:21.689 --> 00:00:24.932
Fluffy, delicious but incredibly wrong.

00:00:24.932 --> 00:00:26.235
These are pancakes.

00:00:26.235 --> 00:00:27.904
They are made in a pan.

00:00:27.904 --> 00:00:29.571
We even have a whole day for them.

00:00:29.571 --> 00:00:31.449
Also, your flapjacks are not flapjacks.

00:00:31.449 --> 00:00:33.075
These are flapjacks.

00:00:33.075 --> 00:00:35.119
Think of a better version
of the granola bar.

00:00:35.119 --> 00:00:36.954
Actually, you're doing
a lot of foods wrong.

00:00:36.954 --> 00:00:39.832
Toast, chips, crisps, bangers.

00:00:39.832 --> 00:00:40.874
Pleasantries.

00:00:40.874 --> 00:00:43.336
You're wasting far too much
time when talking to friends.

00:00:43.336 --> 00:00:44.911
For instance, you see
a mate on the street,

00:00:44.911 --> 00:00:46.547
you go, "All right?" and
they say, "All right?"

00:00:46.547 --> 00:00:47.715
Conversation over.

00:00:47.715 --> 00:00:48.674
It's great, isn't it?

00:00:48.674 --> 00:00:51.177
Instead of listening 20 reasons
why you can't do something,

00:00:51.177 --> 00:00:53.762
just say to your mate,
"I can't be bothered."

00:00:53.762 --> 00:00:55.297
See? Easier.

00:00:55.297 --> 00:00:56.307
Slang.

00:00:56.307 --> 00:00:58.851
Your slang is quite boring and
not nearly confusing enough

00:00:58.851 --> 00:01:01.646
so allow me to kindly explain
using a recent phrase.

00:01:01.646 --> 00:01:03.063
So what is a nandos

00:01:03.063 --> 00:01:04.940
and why is it so cheeky?

00:01:04.940 --> 00:01:06.485
So you're with the lads after a night out

00:01:06.485 --> 00:01:08.393
and you're all like,
"Let's go at Mackey-D's,"

00:01:08.393 --> 00:01:09.478
but your other mate is like,

00:01:09.478 --> 00:01:11.530
"Nah, let's go at chicken nandos instead."

00:01:11.530 --> 00:01:14.129
Everyone is like, "Brilliant,"
so you go have chicken nandos

00:01:14.129 --> 00:01:15.492
and a bit of topnotch
banger with the lads.

00:01:15.492 --> 00:01:16.744
Still confused?

00:01:16.744 --> 00:01:18.704
It's like, say, one night
you're out with your bros

00:01:18.704 --> 00:01:20.664
and you think, "Let's go to MacDonalds."

00:01:20.664 --> 00:01:21.623
Where your friends are like,

00:01:21.623 --> 00:01:23.417
"No dude, got to step it up a notch.

00:01:23.417 --> 00:01:24.752
"Let's go at IHOP."

00:01:24.752 --> 00:01:27.376
You have a great time and
you all go home happy.

00:01:27.376 --> 00:01:28.213
Make sense?

00:01:28.213 --> 00:01:29.256
Great.

00:01:29.256 --> 00:01:31.967
What other things are
Americans doing wrong?

00:01:31.967 --> 00:01:36.889
(classical music)

